<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urraca of León and Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1079–1126</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Queen Urraca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urraca was Queen of León, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> from 1109 to 1126, the daughter and heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a>. Her second marriage, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a>, turned into civil war and was annulled, and she struggled throughout her reign against her husband, the Galician nobility and the supporters of her son. She was succeeded by that son of her first marriage, Alfonso VII.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/urraca-of-leon-and-castile.jpg" alt="Urraca of León and Castile" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UrracaRegina_TumboA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
